  <p>UK activewear brands often need a sourcing partner that can balance premium quality with realistic MOQ. Local production can be useful for small runs, but many UK brands choose China manufacturing when they need broader fabric options, stronger cost control, and scalable private label production.</p>

  <h2>What UK Brands Should Prioritise</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reliable size grading for UK customers.</li>
    <li>Squat-proof leggings and supportive sports bras.</li>
    <li>Clear care labels, fiber content labels, and branded packaging.</li>
    <li>Fast sampling before seasonal drops or influencer campaigns.</li>
    <li>Quality control photos before shipment to the UK.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Private Label vs Full OEM</h2>
  <p>Private label is usually better for UK startups that need to launch quickly with lower risk. Full OEM is better for established brands that already understand their target fit, customer feedback, and reorder volume.</p>

  <div class="market-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Model</th><th>Best For</th><th>Key Benefit</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Private label stock</td><td>Startup launches and boutique gyms</td><td>Lower MOQ and faster timeline</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Custom branding</td><td>Growing DTC brands</td><td>Stronger brand presentation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OEM/ODM</td><td>Established UK brands</td><td>Exclusive fit, fabric, and product identity</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>UK Buyer Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm your target price and margin before sampling.</li>
    <li>Ask for size charts and garment measurements, not only model photos.</li>
    <li>Approve logo method, label artwork, and packaging before bulk production.</li>
    <li>Plan shipping time around collection launch dates.</li>
    <li>Keep first orders focused instead of overbuilding SKU count.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How Fitclo Helps UK Activewear Brands</h2>
  <p>Fitclo supports UK buyers with private label activewear, ready-to-ship styles, custom logo application, fabric selection, sampling, quality control, and export coordination. Our goal is to help UK brands launch collections that look premium without taking unnecessary inventory risk.</p>
